In Java some structures are well described who they should / must be named, e.g. classes.
See the official Java Documentation by Oracle:
https://www.oracle.com/java/technologies/javase/codeconventions-namingconventions.html

As mentioned by Oracle, some structures do not have strict conventions to follow
and just have technical boundaries, e.g. packages. For package names there are
multiple styles seen in the community. Here are some good hints:
https://stackoverflow.com/questions/3179216/what-is-the-convention-for-word-separator-in-java-package-names

As for this project we define our own package naming convention:
1. Every package starts with a _ prefix because it can't start with a number
2. After the _ prefix there comes a number to generate a clear chapter structure
3. In consideration we want better readability, we separate the rest of the package name with _ between each word.